{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implementation language is Go, extending the existing hyperledger/fabric-config library (configtx package) at roughly the referenced commit; all new APIs follow the library's existing get-modify-set ConfigGroup pattern and error conventions.",
    "U1: Add AddConsortium(name) on the consortiums group that creates an empty consortium group; an empty consortium (no orgs) is permitted at the API level since orgs can be added later, and examples will always add orgs after creating the consortium.",
    "U2: Add a function (e.g., NewUnsignedConfigUpdateEnvelope / ComputeConfigUpdate) that returns a *cb.ConfigUpdateEnvelope with no signatures, by refactoring the existing signed-envelope path so the update computation is reusable; the peer channel commands can then sign it externally.",
    "U3: Add ConfigTx.RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses() that deletes the top-level OrdererAddresses value from the channel group; reject attempts to set OrdererAddresses via setters; change new-channel (genesis) creation to omit the top-level field and require each orderer org to specify endpoints at creation time, while leaving endpoints optional on the update path.",
    "U4: Add OrdererGroup.RemoveKafkaBrokers() analogous to RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses, simply deleting the KafkaBrokers value, plus a Kafka-to-EtcdRaft migration example.",
    "U5: Add OrdererGroup.AddConsenter/RemoveConsenter operating on the EtcdRaft consenters list of the channel-level orderer configuration; removal requires exact match of host, port, client TLS cert, and server TLS cert.",
    "U7: Implement individual orderer setters (SetMaxMessageCount, SetAbsoluteMaxBytes, SetPreferredMaxBytes, SetBatchTimeout, SetMaxChannels, SetConsensusType, SetConsensusState) that read the existing orderer values, mutate one field, and write back so sibling values persist; implement SetEtcdRaftMetadata plus individual EtcdRaft options setters (tick/heartbeat/election intervals, max inflight blocks, snapshot interval size) and have the EtcdRaft metadata setter also set ConsensusType to etcdraft (implementer's choice per acceptance criteria); keep GetConfiguration/SetConfiguration intact.",
    "U8: Implement a shared internal MSP helper used by OrdererOrgGroup, ApplicationOrgGroup, and ConsortiumOrgGroup exposing Add/RemoveRootCert, Add/RemoveIntermediateCert, Add/RemoveAdminCert, Add/RemoveCRL, Add/RemoveOUIdentifier, SetCryptoConfig, Add/RemoveTLSRootCert, Add/RemoveTLSIntermediateCert, Set{Client,Peer,Admin,Orderer}OUIdentifier, Enable/DisableNodeOUs; certificates are validated as parseable x509 on add; removals match exact DER bytes; AddCRL/RemoveCRL modify the group's MSP value directly (superseding the standalone CreateMSPCRL flow); GetMSP/SetMSP remain.",
    "U6: Build the CLI as a separate Go binary 'configtx' using cobra-style flags; input files batchUpdate.json, connectionProfile.json (Fabric connection profile format, JSON or YAML), and signingIdentities.json are validated up front with clear errors for unsupported operations; operations stack in order within a single config update per channel.",
    "U6: Use fabric-sdk-go (or equivalent Fabric gRPC clients) with the connection profile and discovery service to locate peers/orderers, fetch each channel's config block, and broadcast the finished config update transaction to the orderer; signing builds a cb.ConfigUpdateEnvelope signed with every provided signing identity and wraps it in a cb.Envelope.",
    "U6: --dryrun computes the per-channel cb.ConfigUpdate and prints it to stdout as JSON (via protolator-style marshaling) without submitting anything, so output can be redirected to a file.",
    "Unit tests are included within each feature activity; CLI end-to-end tests use recorded/generated crypto fixtures and mocked peer/orderer endpoints rather than a long-lived test network."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced Go developer familiar with Hyperledger Fabric performs all work; estimates are effort (work-hours), not elapsed time.",
    "The existing fabric-config codebase, its test harness (cert generation utilities), and CI infrastructure already exist and do not need to be built.",
    "Effort includes implementation and unit tests per activity, plus the example updates explicitly required by U1, U4, U7, and U8; it excludes external code review by other maintainers, release packaging, and performance/security audits.",
    "For U6, updateConsenter and replaceConsenter both target the consenter identified by host/port; replace swaps the full entry and update replaces its TLS certs; unsupported operation names produce a descriptive error and abort processing.",
    "For U6, the tool fetches the current config block per channel, applies all stacked operations to produce one config update transaction per channel, and submits (or prints with --dryrun) each channel's update; 'update MSP requiring one signature' means signing with the single relevant provided admin identity is sufficient.",
    "Certificates and keys in JSON inputs are base64-encoded PEM as shown in the specification; no HSM support is required.",
    "Documentation effort is limited to godoc comments, README, and example code in the repository; no updates to external documentation sites.",
    "The target Fabric version is 2.x (EtcdRaft-capable); no Fabric 1.0 runtime compatibility testing is performed beyond the migration-related functions U3/U4."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A-01",
      "activity_name": "Project setup, codebase study and detailed design",
      "activity_description": "Set up the development environment, study the existing fabric-config/configtx code (channel, orderer, application, consortium, MSP handling, example and test structure), and produce the detailed design for the new APIs and the CLI (function signatures, validation rules, file formats, module layout).",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-02",
      "activity_name": "U1 - AddConsortium API",
      "activity_description": "Implement AddConsortium on the consortiums group including duplicate-name validation and the empty-consortium (no orgs) case; add unit tests; update examples to add a new consortium and then add orgs to it.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-03",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Unsigned ConfigUpdateEnvelope generation",
      "activity_description": "Refactor config update computation so a new public function returns a cb.ConfigUpdateEnvelope without requiring signing identities; keep the existing signed path working; add unit tests verifying an unsigned envelope is produced and can later be signed externally.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-04",
      "activity_name": "U3 - RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses and genesis/orderer-endpoint validation",
      "activity_description": "Implement ConfigTx.RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses; disallow setting the top-level OrdererAddresses value; change new channel/genesis creation to omit the top-level field and require orderer org endpoints at creation (optional on update); add unit tests covering creation, update, and removal paths; update affected examples.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-05",
      "activity_name": "U4 - RemoveKafkaBrokers and Kafka-to-EtcdRaft migration example",
      "activity_description": "Implement OrdererGroup.RemoveKafkaBrokers analogous to legacy orderer address removal; add unit tests; add/improve an example demonstrating migration from Kafka to EtcdRaft including broker cleanup.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-06",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Add/Remove etcdraft consenter APIs",
      "activity_description": "Implement AddConsenter and RemoveConsenter on the orderer configuration's EtcdRaft consenter set, with removal matching all four fields (host, port, client TLS cert, server TLS cert) and duplicate detection on add; add unit tests including partial-match non-removal cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-07",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Individual orderer configuration field setters",
      "activity_description": "Implement SetMaxMessageCount, SetAbsoluteMaxBytes, SetPreferredMaxBytes, SetBatchTimeout, SetMaxChannels, SetConsensusType, SetConsensusState, plus EtcdRaft metadata/options setters (metadata setter also sets consensus type to etcdraft), each preserving existing sibling values via read-modify-write; comprehensive unit tests; update examples to show both the new setter style and the existing GetConfiguration/SetConfiguration style.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-08",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Individual MSP field modifiers for all org group types",
      "activity_description": "Implement the shared MSP helper and expose it on OrdererOrgGroup, ApplicationOrgGroup and ConsortiumOrgGroup: Add/RemoveRootCert, Add/RemoveIntermediateCert, Add/RemoveAdminCert, Add/RemoveCRL, Add/RemoveOUIdentifier, SetCryptoConfig, Add/RemoveTLSRootCert, Add/RemoveTLSIntermediateCert, Set Client/Peer/Admin/Orderer OU identifiers, Enable/DisableNodeOUs (including OU identifier derivation), with x509 validation on add and exact-match removal; extensive unit tests across all three org types; update examples to show both update styles.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-09",
      "activity_name": "U6 - CLI scaffolding and input parsing/validation",
      "activity_description": "Create the 'configtx' CLI binary with the update command and flags (--connectionProfile, --signingIdentities, --dryrun); implement parsing and schema validation for batchUpdate.json (channelList + operations), connectionProfile.json, and signingIdentities.json; produce clear error messages for unsupported operations and malformed input.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-10",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Bulk operations engine",
      "activity_description": "Implement the engine that applies stacked operations (addConsenter, removeConsenter, updateConsenter, replaceConsenter, updateApplicationMSP, updateOrdererMSP, addAnchorPeers, removeAnchorPeers, replaceAnchorPeers) to a fetched channel config using the fabric-config library APIs, computing one config update per channel for the channel list.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-11",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Network connectivity: discovery, config block fetch, update submission",
      "activity_description": "Implement connection-profile-based client setup, use of the discovery service via a peer to resolve orderer endpoints, retrieval of the latest config block for each channel, and broadcast of the finished config update transaction to the orderer, including connection/TLS error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-12",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Signing identities handling and dry-run output",
      "activity_description": "Implement loading of signingIdentities.json, creation of config update signatures per identity, assembly of the signed ConfigUpdateEnvelope/cb.Envelope, and the --dryrun mode that prints the computed per-channel config update as JSON to stdout without submission.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-13",
      "activity_name": "U6 - CLI testing",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for parsing, validation, and each operation, plus end-to-end tests using generated crypto fixtures and mocked peer/orderer endpoints covering multi-channel batches, stacked operations, dry-run output, and error cases.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-14",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting examples and documentation",
      "activity_description": "Final pass over repository examples and documentation: README usage for the new APIs and CLI (including the sample command), godoc comments for all new exported functions, and consistency checks of example code.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A-15",
      "activity_name": "Integration, regression testing, self-review and rework",
      "activity_description": "Run the full test suite and examples end to end, verify interactions between the new APIs (e.g., consenter removal used by the CLI, orderer setters combined with metadata setters), perform self code review, fix defects, and prepare the change for submission.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 230
  }
}

